text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'Add {B}{B}{B}.', 'Arc Lightning deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.', 'At the beginning of the end step, if no creatures are on the battlefield, sacrifice Pestilence.\\n{B}: Pestilence deals 1 damage to each creature and each player.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, each opponent loses 1 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, if an opponent controls more lands than you, you may search your library for up to three basic land cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Choose one —\\n• Target player gains 3 life.\\n• Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', 'Counter target spell.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all enchantments.', "Destroy all lands or all creatures. Creatures destroyed this way can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Drifting Meadow enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Each opponent discards two cards.', 'Each player discards their hand, then draws cards equal to the greatest number of cards a player discarded this way.', 'Each player exiles all creature cards from their graveyard, then sacrifices all creatures they control, then puts all cards they exiled this way onto the battlefield.', 'Each player puts a creature card from their graveyard onto the battlefield.', "Each player returns a creature they control to its owner's hand.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3.\\n{W}: Return enchanted creature to its owner's hand.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and can't block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-1.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever a creature dies, put a +1/+1 counter on enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\nYou control enchanted creature.', 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional one mana of any color.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', "First strike\\nWhen Nekrataal enters the battlefield, destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. That creature can't be regenerated.", 'First strike\\n{W}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Vampire this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Vampire.", 'Flying, haste', 'Flying\\nWhenever Abyssal Specter deals damage to a player, that player discards a card.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target attacking or blocking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Heat Ray deals X damage to target creature.', 'Hurricane deals X damage to each creature with flying and each player.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\n{G}: Regenerate River Boa.", "Lhurgoyf's power is equal to the number of creature cards in all graveyards and its toughness is equal to that number plus 1.", 'Polluted Mire enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Protection from white\\n{1}{R}: Wildfire Emissary gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. You lose life equal to its mana value.', 'Remote Isle enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Return Broken Fall to its owner's hand: Regenerate target creature.", 'Rolling Thunder deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Sacrifice Sanctum Guardian: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to any target this turn, prevent that damage.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Phyrexian Ghoul gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Sandstorm deals 1 damage to each attacking creature.', 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)', 'Shower of Sparks deals 1 damage to target creature and 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Skyshroud Elite gets +1/+2 as long as an opponent controls a nonbasic land.', 'Slippery Karst enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Spike Colony enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Colony: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'Spike Feeder enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Feeder: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Feeder: You gain 2 life.', 'Spike Weaver enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Weaver: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Weaver: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Spike Worker enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Worker: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'Steam Blast deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Syphon Soul deals 2 damage to each other player. You gain life equal to the damage dealt this way.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target player draws four cards.', 'Two target creatures each get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Untap target creature an opponent controls and gain control of it until end of turn. That creature gains haste until end of turn. When you lose control of the creature, tap it.', 'When Cackling Fiend enters the battlefield, each opponent discards a card.', "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever Seasoned Marshal attacks, you may tap target creature.', "Whenever a creature dies, that creature's controller may draw a card.", 'Whenever an opponent plays a land, put a +1/+1 counter on Dirtcowl Wurm.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.', "{0}: Return Blinking Spirit to its owner's hand.", '{1}{G}: Target creature blocks Trumpeting Armodon this turn if able.', '{1}{W}: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn by target attacking creature with flying.', '{2}{G}: Plated Rootwalla gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{B}, Pay 1 life: Sewer Rats gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Activate no more than three times each turn.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Lyrist: Destroy target enchantment.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Regenerate target creature.', '{R}: Regenerate Uthden Troll.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Cinder Marsh doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Vec Townships doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Mogg Hollows doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Thalakos Lowlands doesn't untap during your next untap step.", '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', '{T}: Fire Ants deals 1 damage to each other creature without flying.', '{T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Prodigal Sorcerer deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}: Target attacking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Untap target creature.', '{T}: Untap two target lands.', '{U}: Manta Riders gains flying until end of turn.', '{U}{U}: Tap target creature without flying.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.']
flavor: ['" . . . And the third little boar built his house out of rootwalla plates . . . ."\\n—Skyshroud children\'s story', '". . . But I\'m not tired!"', '"A dash of cool water does wonders to clear a cluttered battlefield."\\n—Vibekke Ragnild, *Witches and War*', '"A skilled decoy can throw your enemies off your trail. A master decoy can survive to do it again."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"Ach! Hans, run! It\'s the lhurgoyf!"\\n—Saffi Eriksdotter, last words', '"And darkness shall be cast from me\\nFor my soul resides in the Sun."\\n—Femeref dirge', '"Beauty to the eye does not always translate to the touch."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"But no one heard the snake\'s gentle hiss for peace over the elephant\'s trumpeting of war."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Children of the Ruins, raised to be warriors, know that life begins when another speaks their names."\\n—Soltari *Tales of Life*', '"Civilization is a conspiracy to disguise the mutilation of nature."\\n—Skyshroud elite creed', '"Death—an outmoded concept. We sleep, and we change."\\n—Sitrik, birth priest', '"Don\'t look at it! Maybe it\'ll go away!"\\n—Ib Halfheart, goblin tactician', '"First blood isn\'t as important as last blood."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"Flourishing during the Ice Age, these wurms were the bane of all Kjeldorans. Their great size and ferocity made them the subject of countless nightmares—they embodied the worst of the Ice Age."\\n—*Kjeldor: Ice Civilization*', '"He cocooned himself alone in his workshop for months. When he finally emerged, all broad grins and excited chatter, I knew he\'d found his answer."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Heel."', '"I always charge a little extra to take on a pegasus. They fly like eagles, kick like mules, and hide like hermits."\\n—Tahli *en*-Dal, bounty hunter', '"I have seen the horrors Kaervek has freed. My Betrayal is certain—but of Kaervek or of Jamuraa, I cannot say."\\n—Jolrael', '"I implore you not to forget the horrors of the past. You would have us start the Brothers\' War anew!"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi heretic', '"I think I used up all my good luck and all my bad luck in the same fall."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"If fear is the only tool you have left, then you\'ll never control me."\\n—Xantcha, to Gix', '"No bird soars too high, if he soars with his own wings."\\n—William Blake,\\n*The Marriage of Heaven and Hell*', '"No fair! Since when does a bug get ta munch on *me*?"\\n—Squee, goblin cabin hand', '"Oi oi oi, me gotta hurt in \'ere,\\nOi oi oi, me smell a ting is near,\\nGonna bosh \'n gonna nosh\\n\'n da hurt\'ll disappear."\\n—Troll chant', '"Protect our mother in her womb."', '"Such rage," thought Vhati, gazing up at the thunderhead from the *Predator*. "It is Greven\'s mind manifest."', '"Teferi is a problem student. Always late for class. No appreciation for constructive use of time."\\n—Barrin, progress report', '"The efreet is a striding storm with a voice that crackles like fire."\\n—Qhattib, vizier of Amiqat', '"The fatal flaw in every plan is the assumption that you know more than your enemy."\\n—Volrath', '"The soldier\'s path is worn smooth by the tread of many feet—all in one direction, none returning."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"The true dishonor for a soldier is surviving the war."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"To fill your mind with knowledge, we must start by emptying it."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Water is firmament to the finned."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"We shun them not for their dream but for their refusal to let such a noble dream die a noble death."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"You will learn to earn death."\\n—Volrath', 'A lightning elemental once killed an entire tribe of merfolk—simply by going for a swim.', 'Although the elves of Argoth always considered them a nuisance, the pixies made fine allies during the war against the machines.', 'At a distance, we mistook the sound for a waterfall . . . .', 'Bring the spear of ancient briar;\\nBring the torch to light the pyre.\\nBring the one who trod our ground;\\nBring the spade to dig his mound.', 'Count carefully the souls and see that none are lost.\\n—Vec teaching', 'Even the landscape turned against Sarsour, first rising up and pelting him, then rearranging itself so he could no longer find his way.', "Few of Rath's rivers follow a steady course, so many new channels are carved for them.", 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', 'If only every message were as perfect as its bearer.', "It's not known whether the Thran built the device to forge their wonders or to defend them.", 'Its windpipe is only the first to amplify its maddening laughter.', "Kerrick's corrupt domain swelled like a blister on Tolaria's skin.", 'Life is eternal. A lifetime is ephemeral.', 'Little dreamt could seem so cruel\\nAs waiting for the wings outspread,\\nThe jagged teeth, the burning eyes,\\nAnd dagger-claws that clench to nerves.', 'Occasionally members of the Institute of Arcane Study acquire a taste for worldly pleasures. Seldom do they have trouble finding employment.', 'One bone broken for every twig snapped underfoot.\\n—Llanowar penalty for trespassing', 'Only by sacrificing any semblance of defense could Gerrard best Greven.', 'Phyrexia wastes nothing. Its food chain is a spiraling cycle.', 'Radiant\'s eyes flashed. "Go, then," the angel spat at Serra, "and leave this world to those who truly care."', "Rainclouds don't last long in Shiv, but that doesn't stop the lightning.", 'Serra told them to guard Urza as he healed. Five years they stood.', 'Sharpen your ears\\n—Elvish expression meaning "grow wiser"', 'The forest was too lush for the brothers to despoil—almost.', "The only sound was the gentle clicking of the faeries' wings. Then those intruders who were still standing turned and fled. One thing was certain: they didn't think the Scryb were very funny anymore.", 'The true names of birds are songs woven into their souls.', 'The viashino had learned how to operate the rig through trial and error—mostly error.', "The viashino knew of the cracked pipes but deliberately left them unmended to bolster the rig's defenses.", 'There are only two rules of tactics: never be without a plan, and never rely on it.', 'These are its last days. But it will not go quietly.', 'These spirits of the air are winsome and wild and cannot be truly contained. Only marginally intelligent, they often substitute whimsy for strategy, delighting in mischief and mayhem.', "They are Phyrexia's couriers; the messages they carry are inscribed on their slick hides.", 'They were formidable even before they learned the use of weapons.', 'Visitors to Shiv fear the dragons, the goblins, or the viashino. Natives fear the ants.', "You lie down with rats, and the rats run away.\\n—Suq'Ata insult"]
